<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's May base metals import prices up.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's May base metals import prices up.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's non-ferrous metals import prices rose in May from the previous month due to gains on the London Metal Exchange (LME), the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Import prices of base metals were as follows:</p>
<p>(US$ price per tonne on CIF)</p>
<p> METAL		     Origin	May     Apr</p>
<p> Copper (99.95 pct)    Chile     2,574     2,470</p>
<p> Copper scrap (berry)  U.S.	2,491     2,348</p>
<p> Aluminium (99.7 pct)  Australia 1,723     1,645</p>
<p> Lead (99.99 pct)	China	 688	 715</p>
<p> Zinc (99.995 pct)     S.America 1,408     1,340</p>
<p> Nickel (99.9 pct)     Canada    7,768     7,574</p>
<p> Tin (99.85 pct)	 Malaysia  5,829     5,761</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
